  "full_text": "So, entertain God and your ass will follow. So, it's hot. Don't get the shirt for the right temperature. So I wonder what Mr. God had to do in evolution about temperature. I wonder if he can tell us any secrets. So the dinosaurs grew feathers and then they learned to fly. I think that's pretty weird. So feathers come from Tree leaves, is that what the consensus is? Pretty strange shit, you know? Juanita. So feathers come from tree leaves, like some DNA got transplanted. It's pretty weird shit. Wonder how that happened. Wow, just think what's gonna happen when humans start doing shit. You think a human could convert a leaf into a feather? That shit sounds pretty hard. What else? Is there any analogy? What about solar panels? I guess we should talk to God a couple times. Mr. God. Skimming the treetops. He himself knows our frame. He is mindful that we are but dust. God is mindful that he created us as finite beings out of a few pounds of garden soil. He understands that. My question is, why don't we understand it? Why do we expect perfection of ourselves and of our associates? You and I become terribly impatient with our own shortcomings and limitations and with each other. We despair because we think we ought to be in spiritual orbit by this time when we're barely skimming the treetops. We think we ought instantly, constantly, and effectively to conquer vast territories for the kingdom, like some spiritual Alexander the Great. And when it doesn't happen, when victory seems elusive, we grow discouraged. Whenever I start feeling like that, I need to revisit the life of Moses. Here was a man who didn't become effective for God until he was 80, long after most of us would be riding a rocking chair or pushing up daisies. Moses began a spiritual career. And guess what? God used him mightily.",
